; ted-prtfile-buffer-overflow (#372): Print builds each printer line in
; charbuff (390 bytes to the end of TED's buffer block of 2438 bytes)
; without a length check; every token becomes ESC[1m + name + ESC[22m.
; blitz2 under inject pad (64 zeroed bytes behind every allocation,
; checked when it is freed), a tokenised file: "x", 27 x "NPrint:"
; (about 420 bytes as printer line), "y".  PRINT into the file
; TEDRUN:work/prt.txt, QUIT (TED frees its buffer block).  Correct:
; nothing is written behind the block; the original writes the printer
; line behind it (inject: "written behind").  Fixed in TED-C: the printer
; line stops silently in front of the token that would not fit.
; @fixed #372
; @file bo.bb2 "x\x00\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:"
; @file bo.bb2 "\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:"
; @file bo.bb2 "\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\xdd\x82:\x00y\x00"
; @source F bo.bb2
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject pad blitz2:blitz2 @FILE@
; @expect file prt.txt "NPrint"
; @expect nostdout "inject: pad: written behind an allocation of 2438 bytes"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 5
wait req "PRINT" "CANCEL"
str 1 "TEDRUN:work/prt.txt"
gad 2
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
